    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "wallet: reject recipient amounts above MAX_MONEY",
    "user": {
      "login": "Bruce039",
      "id": 109469941,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOBoZg9Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/109469941?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Bruce039",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Bruce039/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`CreateTransaction` checks that recipient amounts aren't negative, but not that they're within `MAX_MONEY`. `CreateTransactionInternal` then sums them into `recipients_sum` (spend.cpp:1100) with no range check, and that sum can overflow.\n\nEasiest way to hit it is `fundrawtransaction` with a raw tx that has two outputs of 2^62 sat. It can also be reached with only valid amounts through `walletcreatefundedpsbt`/`send`/`sendmany` and a few thousand 21M BTC outputs. The \"Transaction too large\" check only runs after coin selection, so it doesn't stop this. On master the node aborts:\n\n```\nAssertion failed: (!m_selected_inputs.empty()), function RecalculateWaste, file coinselection.cpp, line 904.\n```\n\nUBSan reports the overflow at spend.cpp:1100 first. With other values the sum wraps to a small positive number instead, and `fundrawtransaction` returns success for a tx with outputs of 46116860184 BTC each.\n\nThis checks every amount and the running sum against `MoneyRange` in `CreateTransaction`, next to the existing negative check, and returns an error before coin selection starts. The new `test_outputs_above_max_money` in `wallet_fundrawtransaction.py` covers a single output above MAX_MONEY, two outputs whose sum is above it, and a sum that overflows int64. On master the first case returns \"Insufficient funds\" and the overflow case crashes the node. With the fix all three get the new error. I ran it on a normal and an ASan/UBSan build, and `wallet_basic.py` and `rpc_psbt.py` still pass.\n",
